Musepack r475: reset the encoder state so a process can encode more than one file

libmpcenc and libmpcpsy keep their state in file-scope variables, and two of
them survive from one encoder to the next:

1. libmpcenc/analy_filter.c defines FASTER, under which Klemm() rearranges
   and negates part of the static table Ci_opt[512] in place.
   mpc_encoder_init() calls Klemm() for every encoder, so from the second
   encoder in the same process on the analysis filter bank runs on a
   scrambled table and the audio comes out damaged. Klemm() now builds its
   tables once per process.

2. libmpcpsy/psy.c tracks the loudness used by AdaptLtq() in a function-scope
   static that Init_Psychoakustik() does not reset, so a second encoder
   starts from the loudness the previous file ended with and writes
   different bytes. The variable is moved to file scope and reset by
   Init_Psychoakustik() together with the other arrays.

With both changes every encoder in a process writes the same bytes as the
first one.

--- a/libmpcenc/analy_filter.c
+++ b/libmpcenc/analy_filter.c
@@ -104,10 +104,17 @@
 void
 Klemm ( void )
 {
+    static int  done = 0;
     int    i;
     int    k;
     float  S [512];
 
+    // The FASTER block below rearranges Ci_opt in place: running it again
+    // would scramble the table, so the tables are built once per process.
+    if ( done )
+        return;
+    done = 1;
+
     for ( i=0; i<32; i++ ) {
         for ( k=0; k<32; k++ ) {
             M [i*32 + k] = (float) cos ( ((2*i+1)*k & 127) * M_PI/64 );
